that granted that there's four games

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:08.860
and then like one bonus mode with like,

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:10.380
where it just says shooting range

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.540
and you shoot, you shoot the targets

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:15.400
without any, without any dressing

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:17.380
like ghosts or xenomorphs.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.020
It's just targets coming out of holes.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.920
But, so that's a total of five different,

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.800
I guess, like backgrounds,

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:29.520
like painted backdrops to do the exact same thing.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.740
It's very, I don't know like what,

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.640
how much of this game costs when it came out,

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.060
but I hope it wasn't full price.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.260
I think that what it's, you know,

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:40.660
what it misses is like,

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:43.200
I think it's nicely like represented

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.120
in those first three light gun games we played,

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:47.900
which were Duck Hunt, Wild Gunman, and...

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:50.440
Hogan's Alley. Hogan's Alley, thank you.

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:53.120
Where like they each kind of gave you

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:55.480
like a different reason to play a light gun game.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.960
Whereas like Duck Hunt was all about aim.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:01.660
Hogan's Alley was all about like decision making,

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.720
quick decision making. And Wild Gunman was all about like reflexes

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:07.280
and reaction time. Whereas this just doesn't,

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:11.880
I mean, I guess this is about aim also,

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.600
but like worse than Duck Hunt.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:15.780
It looks like, I mean,

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:17.600
was it easier than Duck Hunt or was it harder?

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:18.580
It was way easier.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:20.720
Yeah, it looks easier.

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.280
The problem is, like you're saying,

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.620
in Duck Hunt, it's about aim

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:26.500
because the ducks move sporadically across the screen,

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:28.780
but also like diagonally, left to right.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.140
They appear in and out.

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.320
Here, because you're, I mean,

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:34.040
like I guess like the ghosts and the vampires

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:36.380
are somewhat of an exception to that.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.240
And, you know, I'm saying for the most part,

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:41.040
the enemies just move horizontally across the screen.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:43.000
And if you give them enough time,

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.980
then they'll shoot back at you or whatever.

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:47.000
But otherwise it's, you know,

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:48.680
it's a straight shot to set up.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:51.180
You just have to be prepared for them to appear on the screen.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:55.580
Yeah, yeah. I just think that if, yeah,

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.860
if a game is going to use the light gun,

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.680
it seems so far from what we've seen.

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:01.260
We've gotten a couple others that I liked,

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:03.380
but I feel like if a game is going to use the light gun,

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:06.680
it needs to do something unique

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:09.420
or just something interesting and different, you know?

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.700
Like there's, I feel like the light gun

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:15.540
is not a game in and of itself.

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:16.640
And I feel like some of these developers

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.660
seem to think that like,

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:18.920
hey, as long as you can aim and shoot,

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:22.840
we can make a game. But like, I feel like it does need a good reason

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:26.420
to like deserve light gun use.

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:28.240
Yeah. Right.

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.480
And it's kind of bizarre that, you know,

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:33.660
the three games that you mentioned are 1985 games.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.660
And I wouldn't just say that like,

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:38.600
they're stronger from a gameplay perspective.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:41.480
I think the presentations are even better in like,

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.200
say, let's just use Hogan's Alley

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.340
as an example there, right?

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:46.520
Because they're kind of trying to do the same thing,

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:47.440
like a shooting range.

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:51.000
Granted that Hogan's Alley is more of like a test of decision making

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.460
on you make sure you don't kill the good people.

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:55.820
But like that was done,

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:59.920
like so smart from a perspective of having it be at a,

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:01.800
like FBI training headquarters

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.700
and everybody being cardboard cutouts.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.660
And you have to wait for them to appear, you know?

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:10.420
Here, all of that is lost in favor of like,

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:15.880
what looks like those first rounds of like third party games

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:19.560
that we were getting when people started making games for the NES.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:23.460
This one just feels like it's jumping into the party so late,

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:27.860
but missing all of the directions that the Zapper has gone in since.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:30.020
I mean, you have Duck Hunt, Hogan's Alley,

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.320
and Wild Gummen laid down the like blueprint, right?

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:33.760
But then you had Gumshoe,

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:35.340
which tried something completely different

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:38.720
and tried to do like a platformer with the Zapper.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:43.260
And even Gotcha, you know, made it into like a-

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.600
Gotcha the sport, yes. Yeah, made it into like a competitive,

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.880
like sporting thing with paintball and stuff.

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:49.900
Freedom Force and Operation Wolf.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.680
Operation Wolf's an essential game right now.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.540
And both of those took everything that we liked about Duck Hunt,

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:56.700
Hogan's Alley, and Wild Gummen

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.520
and put like a narrative over them

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:01.660
and made it a more like cohesive experience

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.180
where like the levels get tougher

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:06.940
and you have to use all three of those skills,

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:10.240
decision-making, aim, and reflexes.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.780
Very time crisis-y.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:15.220
Right, exactly. Shooting range goes back on all of that

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:17.480
and instead makes like the equivalent

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:19.400
of like a modern day plug-and-play game.

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:23.440
Yeah, this is definitely regressive, I would say,

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:28.120
in terms of game design and just effort, it seems.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:32.380
I don't really know what else to say about this game.

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:34.160
I have something to say.

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:36.200
It's surprising, okay?

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.640
You know, sometimes you guys are shocked

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.420
when I don't have all the information.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:45.720
I remember, Sean, recently I didn't get to like the end,

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:47.120
I didn't know how like the game ended

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:47.980
and you were like, what do you mean?

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.480
You're like the host of the show, right?

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.360
And I agree, that's my problem.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:52.380
Like I should have known.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:54.880
However, it's even more concerning

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.780
when I feel like Wikipedia doesn't know what's going on.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.720
And I went to shooting range.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.900
