00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:07.600
but I wouldn't assume,

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:10.180
unless the ghost is wearing a cowboy hat

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:12.380
and I missed it. Well, it definitely, I mean, look at,

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:13.660
if you look at the stuff,

00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:16.800
like it's definitely like in the desert

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:20.180
and ish,

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.800
because it's not green on the ground.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.520
I mean, that said, there is an inexplicably evil looking

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:30.280
like tree in the background,

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:31.620
which isn't very western,

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:34.560
but it kind of looks like old westy.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:38.140
Yeah, I thought it looked like a haunted saloon

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:40.280
or something. Yeah. All right, all right.

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:41.660
Conceding even that,

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:44.360
the sentence still just doesn't even make sense.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:46.780
Even though people did not land on the moon

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:47.720
until the 1960s,

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:49.040
the game came out in 1989.

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:52.620
All right? That's the 20th anniversary

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.540
of the landing on the moon.

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:56.260
Oh, there it is.

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:57.360
So, if anything,

00:21:57.760 --> 00:21:59.640
you know, every game should feature the moon

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:00.740
by that logic.

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:04.460
No, that's a great,

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:05.840
that was a great,

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:06.960
that's one of my favorite sentences

00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.380
on Wikipedia. Yeah.

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:10.420
And this is supposed to be a party game,

